{! Connecting to the proxies of a target fails as connecting to the host behind each does when its name does not
   resolve. The application reaches a proxied target by the address of its proxy, so it looks no name up; the
   failure is raised where its lookup would have failed, before a connection is made.

   $1 is the address connected to. An InetSocketAddress prints as hostname/address:port, with an empty host name
   when it has none, so both forms end with /{proxyHost}:port.

   Every rule that throws records that it fired by setting the system property {hit}, and is followed by one that,
   on the way out of the method, takes the frames of the agent off the exception; see hide-frames.btm. !}
{#for proxy in proxies}

# the channels of java.nio, which Netty and with it Vert.x connect through
RULE {fault} SocketChannel.connect to {proxy.port}
CLASS sun.nio.ch.SocketChannelImpl
METHOD connect(java.net.SocketAddress)
AT ENTRY
IF $1.toString().endsWith("/{proxyHost}:{proxy.port}")
DO java.lang.System.setProperty("{hit}", "true");
   throw new java.net.UnknownHostException("{proxy.host}: Name or service not known")
ENDRULE
RULE {fault} SocketChannel.connect to {proxy.port}: hide the frames of the agent
CLASS sun.nio.ch.SocketChannelImpl
METHOD connect(java.net.SocketAddress)
AT EXCEPTION EXIT
IF true
DO io.quarkiverse.resiliencytesting.runtime.internal.jvm.InjectedFrames.hide($^)
ENDRULE

# the sockets of java.net, which JDBC drivers connect through
RULE {fault} Socket.connect to {proxy.port}
CLASS sun.nio.ch.NioSocketImpl
METHOD connect(java.net.SocketAddress, int)
AT ENTRY
IF $1.toString().endsWith("/{proxyHost}:{proxy.port}")
DO java.lang.System.setProperty("{hit}", "true");
   throw new java.net.UnknownHostException("{proxy.host}: Name or service not known")
ENDRULE
RULE {fault} Socket.connect to {proxy.port}: hide the frames of the agent
CLASS sun.nio.ch.NioSocketImpl
METHOD connect(java.net.SocketAddress, int)
AT EXCEPTION EXIT
IF true
DO io.quarkiverse.resiliencytesting.runtime.internal.jvm.InjectedFrames.hide($^)
ENDRULE
{/for}
